cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "藏文三大方言 G2P (Tibetan Three Dialects G2P): Rule-based Grapheme-to-Phoneme for the three major Tibetan dialects"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, rule-based grapheme-to-phoneme (G2P) converter for written Tibetan
  that produces Montreal Forced Aligner (MFA) lexicon-format pronunciations for the
  three major dialect groups — Ü-Tsang (Lhasa), Khams (Dergé), and Amdo (Labrang).
authors:
  - family-names: "Khepa-Nyima"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-23
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/Khepa-Nyima/tibetan-three-dialects-g2p"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Khepa-Nyima/tibetan-three-dialects-g2p"
keywords:
  - Tibetan
  - grapheme-to-phoneme
  - G2P
  - text-to-speech
  - TTS
  - forced alignment
  - MFA
  - low-resource languages
  - phonetics
  - Ü-Tsang
  - Khams
  - Amdo
